  "description": {
   "value": "<p><strong>Cost:</strong> 100eb (Premium) <strong>♦</strong> <strong>Required Slots:</strong> 0</p>\n<p><strong>Fits:</strong> All Melee Weapons, individual eligibility by weapon category</p>\n<p><em>Getting up close is dangerous. That’s why humanity made longer poles, handles, chains, whips, flails, and balanced throwing knives. Thanks, us.</em></p>\n<p>Only one Melee Range Modification may be installed. The range at which the weapon can make Melee Attacks and the Range Table it uses for Throwing is changed to match that of the Melee Range Modification. Damage is unaffected. Melee Weapons with a Long or Very Long Handle cannot be Concealed and cannot be installed into Popup Melee Cyberware. Melee Weapons with a Very Long Handle have their ROF reduced to ROF 1 and require BODY 14+ to be wielded One-Handed.</p>\n<p><strong>▶</strong> <strong>Light/Medium Melee Weapon</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Throwing Handle</strong>  — None / Shortbow</p>\n<p><strong>Short Handle (default</strong>) — Melee Range</p>\n<p><strong>Long Handle</strong>  — 4m/yds</p>\n<p><strong>Very Long Handle</strong> — 6m/yds / Bow</p>\n<p><strong>Chain Handle</strong> — 10m/yds / None</p>\n<p><strong>▶</strong> <strong>Heavy/Very Heavy Melee Weapon</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Short Handle (default)</strong> — Melee Range</p>\n<p><strong>Long Handle</strong>  — 4m/yds</p>\n<p><strong>Very Long Handle</strong>  — 6m/yds / Bow</p>\n<p><strong>Attachment slots:</strong> 0</p>\n<p><em>From <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13EnSAoiLDsC7zmL-Jr1RqIh_EnuVuFnExqiipDVquMk/edit\">Corgo's 77 Collection V3</a> by Corgopolis (Weapons &gt; Attachment Catalog &gt; Grips &amp; Controls).</em></p>"
